      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This report summarizes the clinical frequencies of systemic hypertension and necropsy evidence of cardiomegaly in various cardiovascular conditions (Table I), termed \"the hypertensive diseases\" because of their frequent association with systemic hypertension. Although long recognized as a major risk factor, systemic hypertension appears to be an even greater risk factor to the development of various cardiovascular conditions than previously appreciated. Hypertension by itself appears to be the sole underlying factor in most cases of nontraumatic cerebral arterial or aortic (dissection = partial rupture) rupture. In association with hyperlipidemia, hypertension clearly accelerates atherosclerosis and its devastating consequences."},
